     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and the maximum for a single dose is about 1,000  mg. At this dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the usual maximum.\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, which is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO** at some other frequency.\n\nIf 1700 mg three times daily is what you intend, please confirm that explicitly. If you want, I can add a note with your rationale to the order. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
